            answer: "(a) Clinic: TP = 0.10 × 0.562 = 0.0562; FP = 0.90 × 0.055 = 0.0495; PPV = 0.0562 / 0.1057 ≈ 53%. Screening: TP = 0.0001 × 0.562 = 0.0000562; FP = 0.9999 × 0.055 ≈ 0.0550; PPV ≈ 0.10%, about 1 true cancer for every 980 positive results. (b) The study chose its groups, so 687 of 2997 participants (23%) had cancer; PPV rises with prevalence. In a screened population almost every positive result would be false, and the test also misses about half of early cancers, so CA 19-9 cannot be used for screening.",
